Package: statci
Title: Statistical CI/CD, Calibration Fuzzing, and Manuscript Auditing
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Marcus", "Harris", , "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Provides automated continuous integration and verification tools for
    statistical R pipelines and manuscripts. Includes a 20-rule abstract syntax
    tree (AST) statistical linter for R scripts and 'Quarto'/'RMarkdown'
    documents with incremental Git-diff pull-request linting and 'SARIF' 2.1.0
    export, an estimator calibration and simulation-based calibration (SBC;
    Talts et al., 2018 <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1804.06788>) fuzzing harness with
    exact Clopper-Pearson bounds <doi:10.1093/biomet/26.4.404>, power-curve and
    parallel RNG invariance auditing, a manuscript-to-model consistency auditor
    for 'Quarto', 'RMarkdown', and 'LaTeX' prose and tables, an adversarial
    sensitivity and multiverse specification-curve robustness suite, project
    configuration orchestration, standalone HTML and Markdown audit reports,
    and a 'GitHub Actions' workflow generator.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://marcusharrisphd.com/statci/, https://github.com/MarcusHarrisUConn/statci
BugReports: https://github.com/MarcusHarrisUConn/statci/issues
